WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.096
For APQN 2026 at Symbiosis International University, Sarthak Gore built the conference website and paper submission portal.

2
00:00:07.096 --> 00:00:14.710
The conference received more than fifty papers and more than two hundred registrations from national and international participants.

3
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:20.479
The digital workflow covered paper collection, review, delegate registration, and payment reporting.

4
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:24.344
Some submitted papers were selected; no acceptance rate is claimed.

5
00:00:25.044 --> 00:00:29.738
My individual contribution was the conference website and paper submission portal.

6
00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:32.772
The IT team implemented the BillDesk payment gateway.

7
00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:38.496
The transaction dashboard was a joint effort, with approximately equal contributions from me and IT.

8
00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:42.960
I also prepared transaction reports and dashboards for management and finance.

9
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.284
This case study credits the payment integration to IT and the dashboard to our collaboration.

10
00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:57.489
The paper portal guides authors through paper details, author information, corresponding-author consent, co-authors, file uploads, and declarations.

11
00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:00.822
The demonstrated entry screen uses an emailed access code.

12
00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:05.534
Abstracts are limited to two hundred words, and Word manuscripts to ten megabytes.

13
00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:16.223
On submission, the system creates a paper identifier, stores structured records in Google Sheets and documents in Google Drive, and emails an acknowledgement to the corresponding author.

14
00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:19.844
Administrators assign submitted papers to reviewers.

15
00:01:19.844 --> 00:01:25.966
Reviewers download their assigned papers and record acceptance or rejection, with an optional author message.

16
00:01:25.966 --> 00:01:31.864
In the reviewed source, reviewer decisions are released directly and emailed to the corresponding author.

17
00:01:31.864 --> 00:01:35.290
Administrators can request revisions before a final decision.

18
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:41.076
When a revision is requested, a new document version can be uploaded while previous files are retained.

19
00:01:41.076 --> 00:01:44.053
Authors can track their status and released feedback.

20
00:01:44.753 --> 00:01:49.687
The general registration form collects national and international delegate details.

21
00:01:49.687 --> 00:01:55.692
Payment categories distinguish APQN members from non-members, and local from international delegates.

22
00:01:55.692 --> 00:02:01.519
The form applies early-bird or regular prices and selects Indian rupees or US dollars accordingly.

23
00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:04.016
Participants may add a half-day excursion.

24
00:02:04.016 --> 00:02:11.091
A separate form serves the SIU community, including staff, faculty, and students, with employee or student identifiers.

25
00:02:11.791 --> 00:02:16.109
After registration, participants review the fee summary and proceed to BillDesk.

26
00:02:16.109 --> 00:02:19.995
The IT team implemented the gateway integration for the payment journey.

27
00:02:19.995 --> 00:02:26.093
Following a successful payment, the participant receives an email confirmation with the payment receipt attached.

28
00:02:26.093 --> 00:02:34.351
The shared administrative dashboard links registration information with payment records so the team can check transaction outcomes and support enquiries.

29
00:02:35.051 --> 00:02:39.485
The transaction dashboard was jointly developed by Sarthak and the IT team.

30
00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:46.640
It shows successful, failed, and active transactions, with filters and a facility to retrieve the latest BillDesk status.

31
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.192
The team uses it to cross-check saved records against the BillDesk dashboard.

32
00:02:51.192 --> 00:02:55.154
Every number and record shown here is fictional demonstration data.

33
00:02:55.154 --> 00:02:59.056
No confidential participant or transaction details are reproduced.

34
00:02:59.756 --> 00:03:04.553
Active transactions represent payment journeys that participants left incomplete.

35
00:03:04.553 --> 00:03:07.395
The team follows up and shares the payment link.

36
00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:12.844
Once the participant completes payment, the successful outcome is verified against BillDesk.

37
00:03:12.844 --> 00:03:20.424
Registration reports connect participant details with payment status, while the staff report offers CSV, Excel, and PDF exports.

38
00:03:20.424 --> 00:03:25.280
These records supported the financial reports prepared for management and finance.

39
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.484
All confidential dashboard examples in this walkthrough use dummy data.
